    {
      "id": "claim_8bc640fca662420f935f442c05d8b5ab",
      "statement": "Revenue Procedure 2025-41 applies to taxable years beginning “on or after” 2026-01-01: its AMT exemption is $90,100 for an unmarried individual and $140,200 for married joint filers or surviving spouses, its phase-out thresholds are $500,000 and $1,000,000 respectively, and those thresholds are not indexed before taxable years beginning 2030-01-01.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://bulletins/IRS/2025-08-rev-proc-2025-41-amt-thresholds.md#L8-L22",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:77e48bf911b3febcc0dd734eaf9a5a2de337677e1e61b5a7af01d9da42c6a324:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1b51618ceed347a89c0071652a4600a6",
      "statement": "For a specified private activity bond—defined for this purpose as a section 141 private activity bond issued after 1986-08-07 with section 103 tax-exempt interest—interest remains an “item of tax preference” included in alternative minimum taxable income, and Revenue Procedure 2025-41 does not modify that definition or treatment.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://bulletins/IRS/2025-08-rev-proc-2025-41-amt-thresholds.md#L24-L28",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8d9c4266428c6a1d221c563364e8f1a0b3d9d6aefaefcdd9883319af1c9f655c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_74b04ecb116d40cd964f20fc8fdbfc64",
      "statement": "Revenue Procedure 2025-41 explicitly preserves the qualified-501(c)(3) exception: interest on a qualified section 145 bond is not an AMT preference or part of alternative minimum taxable income, while the municipal research says nonprofit hospitals and private higher education are predominantly qualified 501(c)(3) bonds and airport special-facility paper predominantly is not.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://bulletins/IRS/2025-08-rev-proc-2025-41-amt-thresholds.md#L30-L34",
